      "passed": false,
      "description": "Sortino >= 1.5: risk-adjusted return against downside volatility only. Sharpe punishes upside jumps; Sortino does not, so positively-skewed (trend-style) edges are judged on their pain, not their lottery tickets. For symmetric returns Sortino ~= sqrt(2) x Sharpe, so 1.5 is calibrated to the same elite bar as OOS Sharpe > 1.0. A secondary gate \u2014 DSR stays the primary statistical gate because the multiple-testing deflation math is built for Sharpe and has no clean Sortino analogue."
